  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/civil-rights-movement> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The mass struggle, led and sustained above all by Black Americans, to end legal segregation and racial discrimination and secure equal citizenship and voting rights; its best-known phase ran from the mid-1950s to 1968 and produced the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Voting Rights Act of 1965 and the Fair Housing Act of 1968." .
