<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "No Japanese American was convicted of serious espionage or sabotage during the war; the rumours cited by the Army were unverified, and Congress later found the policy was driven by racial prejudice, war hysteria and a failure of political leadership." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "Japanese Americans were removed and imprisoned because they were caught spying or committing sabotage, so the camps were a military necessity." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "The government justified the removal as military necessity at the time, the Supreme Court accepted that claim in 1944, and the word \"evacuation\" made forced removal sound like protection." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why do the National Park Service and many historians prefer \"incarceration\" and \"forced removal\" to \"internment\" and \"evacuation\"?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Internment is a law-of-war term for detaining enemy nationals, which the Justice Department and Army did separately to non-citizens; most people in the ten WRA camps were U.S. citizens held without charges, and \"evacuation\" wrongly suggests being moved out of danger." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the government justify the removal, and what does the evidence show?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "General DeWitt and President Roosevelt claimed military necessity, citing reports of signals and sabotage; those reports were unverified, the FBI's director mocked the Army's intelligence as hysterical, and no Japanese American was convicted of serious espionage or sabotage." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the Supreme Court's two December 1944 decisions differ?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "In Korematsu it upheld the exclusion order 6–3 as a military necessity, while in Ex parte Endo it ruled that the government could not keep detaining citizens it conceded were loyal; the exclusion orders were lifted effective January 2, 1945." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What did the redress movement achieve, and how?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Japanese American organizations pressed Congress, which created a commission in 1980; its findings and recommendations led to the Civil Liberties Act of 1988, which apologized, paid $20,000 to each surviving incarcerated person (82,219 people in all) and funded public education." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The West Coast exclusion orders are lifted." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1945-01-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tule Lake closes, the last of the ten WRA camps; the WRA is disbanded on June 30, 1946." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1946-03-20"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A federal court in San Francisco vacates Fred Korematsu's conviction, citing government misconduct." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/12> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1983-11-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "President Ronald Reagan signs the Civil Liberties Act of 1988, with an apology and $20,000 for each surviving incarcerated person." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/13> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1988-08-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Japan attacks Pearl Harbor; a presidential proclamation makes Japanese nationals in the U.S. liable to be detained as enemy aliens." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1941-12-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "President Franklin D. Roosevelt signs Executive Order 9066, letting military commanders designate areas from which any person may be excluded." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1942-02-19"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Executive Order 9102 creates the War Relocation Authority (WRA) to run the camps." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1942-03-18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Public Law 503 makes violating an exclusion order a federal crime." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1942-03-21"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The first Civilian Exclusion Order removes Japanese Americans from Bainbridge Island, Washington." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1942-03-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Army activates the 442nd Regimental Combat Team, combining the 100th Battalion with mainland Nisei volunteers." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1943-02-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The WRA begins giving incarcerated adults the so-called loyalty questionnaire." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/7> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1943-02-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Tule Lake is designated a segregation center for people the government labeled disloyal." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1943-07-31"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Supreme Court upholds exclusion in Korematsu v. United States but rules in Ex parte Endo that loyal citizens cannot be held." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration/timeline/9> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1944-12-18"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/japanese-american-incarceration> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
