<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "The marchers had agreed not to carry firearms or clubs, the state's historical marker and a National Park Service study describe them as unarmed, and over a dozen marchers were shot in the back while fleeing; exactly how the first shots came is still debated." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "The \"Lattimer riots\" were a violent uprising by armed foreign miners that deputies had to put down." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Early newspaper accounts came largely from the sheriff and coal-company sympathizers, the trial records have been lost, and nativist hostility toward Slavic immigrants made the \"riot\" label easy to accept, so some newspapers still used it in the 1930s." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why were the Lattimer marchers on strike, and why were immigrant miners especially vulnerable in 1897?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "They were protesting low wages, high prices for supplies the company sold them and abuses by company-town staff. As recent Polish, Slovak and Lithuanian immigrants, none of them citizens, they faced nativist hostility, a new state tax on employers of non-citizens, and a sheriff's posse drawn from Anglo-American townspeople and company agents." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did a massacre that ended in acquittals end up strengthening the miners' union?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "The killings united the region's immigrant communities and disproved the idea that Slavic and Italian workers were docile; within four months more than 15,000 anthracite workers joined the United Mine Workers, which under John Mitchell led the 1900 and 1902 strikes that brought presidential intervention." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did the Lattimer massacre fade from national memory, and how was it revived?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Scholars point to the victims' ethnicity, nativist attitudes, the site's rural remoteness and coal operators' interest in forgetting. Interest revived in the civil rights era, leading to a 1972 memorial dedicated with Cesar Chavez, centennial markers in 1997 and an archaeological survey in 2010." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pennsylvania enacts the Campbell Act, a tax of three cents a day on coal operators for each non-citizen they employ." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1897-08-21"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sheriff James Martin's deputies fire on about 400 marching strikers near Lattimer, killing nineteen and wounding dozens." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1897-09-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Martin and his deputies go on trial for murder at the Luzerne County Courthouse in Wilkes-Barre." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1898-02-01"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The jury acquits all the defendants." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1898-03-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A UMW-led anthracite strike of about 125,000 workers ends." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1900-10-29"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Miners return to work after the five-month anthracite strike of 1902." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1902-10-23"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A memorial boulder and state marker are dedicated at Lattimer; Cesar Chavez speaks." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/7> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1972-09-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The centennial is marked with new state markers and remarks in the Congressional Record." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1997-09-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "University of Maryland archaeologists and local volunteers survey the massacre site with metal detectors." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre/timeline/9> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "2010"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Event> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Lattimer massacre" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Lattimer Massacre of 1897" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Lattimer riots" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/labor-history-of-the-united-states> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The killing of at least nineteen unarmed striking coal miners, nearly all Polish, Slovak and Lithuanian immigrants, by a Luzerne County sheriff's posse on the road to Lattimer, Pennsylvania, on September 10, 1897; the sheriff and his deputies were acquitted, and the killings drove thousands of anthracite miners into the United Mine Workers." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/scheme/economy-and-work> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Lattimer massacre" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/coal-and-iron-police> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/lattimer-massacre> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/great-railroad-strike-of-1877> .
