  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/panic-of-1873> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A financial crisis that began when the railroad-financing bank Jay Cooke and Company failed on September 18, 1873, closed the New York Stock Exchange for ten days, and set off a depression that lasted until about 1879, ruining thousands of businesses, sinking the Freedman's Savings Bank and helping to turn national politics away from Reconstruction." .
