<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/misconception> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#Misconception> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "No record gives the day. Douglass believed he was born about 1817; a ledger kept by his enslaver Aaron Anthony notes February 1818, possibly added later, and Douglass chose February 14 to celebrate." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "Douglass was born on February 14, 1818, a birthday recorded at the time." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Enslaved people were routinely denied knowledge of their own birthdays, and the uncertainty is itself evidence of what slavery took from them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did publishing his Narrative in 1845 put Douglass in danger, and how was that danger resolved?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "The book named the people and places of his enslavement, exposing him as a fugitive who could be seized; he toured Britain and Ireland, where supporters raised $711.66 to buy his freedom from Hugh Auld, so he returned to the United States legally free in 1847." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did Douglass's view of the Constitution change, and why does it matter?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "He first held William Lloyd Garrison's view that the Constitution was a proslavery compact, but between about 1848 and 1852 came to read it as an antislavery document; that let him work through politics and the law against slavery and broke his alliance with Garrison." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why did Douglass support the Fifteenth Amendment even though it did not enfranchise women?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "He backed women's suffrage, but argued in 1869 that for Black Americans in the former slave states the vote was a matter of life and death, so Black men's voting rights could not wait for a separate women's amendment." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/10> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Delivers \"What to the Slave Is the Fourth of July?\" at Corinthian Hall, Rochester." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/10> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1852-07-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/11> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Meets President Lincoln to protest unequal pay and treatment of Black soldiers." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/11> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1863-08-10"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/12> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "At the American Equal Rights Association meeting, argues that Black men's voting rights are a matter of life and death." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/12> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1869-05-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/13> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Appointed U.S. marshal for the District of Columbia by President Hayes." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/13> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1877"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/14> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/14> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Appointed U.S. minister resident and consul general to Haiti, serving until 1891." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/14> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1889"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/15> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/15> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Dies at Cedar Hill, his Washington home, after attending a meeting of the National Council of Women." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/15> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1895-02-20"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Born Frederick Augustus Washington Bailey in Talbot County, Maryland, according to a later ledger notation; he himself believed he was born about 1817." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1818-02"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Sent to Baltimore to live with Hugh and Sophia Auld, where he begins learning to read." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1826"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hired out to Edward Covey, a so-called slave breaker, and fights back against his beatings." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1834"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Escapes to New York disguised as a sailor, using a free Black sailor's papers and a ticket paid for by Anna Murray." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1838-09-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/5> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Marries Anna Murray in New York; the couple settles in New Bedford, Massachusetts, as the Douglasses." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/5> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1838-09-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Hired as a lecturer by the Massachusetts Anti-Slavery Society." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1841"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Publishes Narrative of the Life of Frederick Douglass and begins a lecture tour of Britain and Ireland." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/7> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1845"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Returns legally free after supporters pay Hugh Auld $711.66; launches the North Star in Rochester, New York." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1847"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/9> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Seconds Elizabeth Cady Stanton's suffrage resolution at the Seneca Falls women's rights convention." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass/timeline/9> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1848-07"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYearMonth> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
