  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/frederick-douglass> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An abolitionist, orator, editor and public official (c. 1818–1895) who escaped slavery in Maryland in 1838 and became the most prominent Black American voice of the nineteenth century, campaigning against slavery, for Black citizenship and voting rights, and for women's rights." .
