  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/6> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "The Walking Purchase begins; proprietary agents use an unsigned 1686 draft deed to take perhaps over a million acres of Lenape land." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/6> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1737-09-19"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/7> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Mason and Dixon survey the boundary with Maryland." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/7> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1767"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#TimelineEntry> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/8> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Pennsylvania adopts its first state constitution, with a one-house Assembly and no governor." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/pennsylvania/timeline/8> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#date> "1776-09-28"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
